Expected elements: present

Backbone drawn: fixed nav, breadcrumb, footer with product line, three links, disclosure, all three marks. Exactly one provenance marker — the `Data` row, `Synthetic demo data`. No Debug button, no disabled control, no empty panel. The decoded-input section carries no 'supply an ABI' action; I record that present-by-design rather than missing, because §1 forbids a control that cannot succeed and the note now says so.

The changes: (a) landed in half. RAW (687,1008) no longer prints `0x` and no longer offers a copy affordance — it prints an em dash. But SELECTOR above prints `0x1a2b3c4d`, so the shared emptiness test is never exercised here and the two rows read as a contradiction (finding 1). (b) is not observable here: the only cost label is `COST · MANA`, unchanged, and the label column is uppercase, so a humanised string still renders `COST · TRANSACTION FEE`. (c) landed in its second half verbatim — "An ABI would not help, and BlockTracer cannot yet be given one in any case" — but the opener reads "This selector is not in any ABI BlockTracer holds…", not the claimed "BlockTracer holds no call data…".

Of the carried P2s four stand (chip rung, AGE sentence, section rules, hero finality). The H1/H2 collapse does not: 24px figure height against 17px cap is a genuine 1.4x step, downgraded to P3 for the weight inversion alone.

Fixes: give SELECTOR and RAW one absence vocabulary; take the AGE statement out of the token chip.

Rating: 6/10

